# Copy this to ~/.munim/.env, which is the location that always works: the MCP
# server is spawned by your coding agent and inherits neither your shell nor
# your working directory. A .env in the directory you run from also works, and
# an exported environment variable beats both. `munim doctor` says which file
# it read.
#
# Model host. Only needed if you turn agents on, which is off by default:
#   munim config ai on
# The key can go here or in your keychain (`munim config ai key gemini`), and
# the keychain has no folder, so it works from any directory.
#
# MUNIM_AI is deliberately NOT read from this file. python-dotenv writes into
# the process environment permanently and the MCP server loads once at startup,
# so a switch set here would go sticky and silently beat every later
# `munim config ai on`. Use the command; `munim doctor` says if one is here.
#
# Bedrock ships with strands-agents and works out of the box. Gemini and
# Anthropic are Strands extras, so they need an install of their own:
#   pip install 'munim[gemini]'
# Without it, those hosts cannot be constructed at all, whatever key is set.

# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# MUNIM_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Which host to use. `auto` tries bedrock, then gemini, then anthropic, and
# skips any that is not installed or has no credential.
# MUNIM_AI_HOST=gemini

# Bedrock, if you have access:
# AWS_PROFILE=hackathons
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# MUNIM_BEDROCK_MODEL=us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0

# Fallback:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# OAuth apps. One registration per provider serves every client you connect:
# these identify Munim to the provider, not a client. Redirect URL is
# http://localhost:8976/oauth/callback for all of them. Without these,
# `munim connect` falls back to pasting an API key.

# VERCEL_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# VERCEL_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# CLOUDFLARE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# CLOUDFLARE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# SUPABASE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# SUPABASE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Providers whose authorization server will not register a client on demand.
# Every Google MCP server is one: accounts.google.com advertises no
# registration endpoint and requires a secret, so an application has to be
# registered by hand at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials.
# Choose the "Desktop app" type: its redirect is http://localhost and Google
# documents its secret as not confidential, which is how every CLI ships one.
#
# GMAIL_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GMAIL_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# STITCH_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# STITCH_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
